<title>UK: UK plans heavier fines on oil-discharging ships.</title>
<headline>UK plans heavier fines on oil-discharging ships.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain is to raise the maximum fine its magistrates may impose for illegal discharges of oil by ships into the sea five-fold to 250,000 stg, junior transport minister Glenda Jackson said on Friday.</p>
<p>A spokeswoman in Jackson's department said the higher fines were expected to take effect from September.</p>
<p>Jackson said in a written parliamentary answer that Britain was pressing for the international designation of all waters around its shores as a special area in which discharges from oil tankers would be banned. -- London Newsroom +44 171 5427767</p>
</text>
